  "body": "The Sodick wire post of issue 617 was written from Sodick's 1998 \"Wire EDM Machine Operation\" manual (Mark 21 / EX21 control). The machine of issue 617 is an AQ600L with a later LN-series control. No free official programming reference for the LN controls was found on the open web, so whether they read the 1998 words unchanged is unconfirmed, and so is the form their programs take around the cut (condition and offset table rows at the head of the file, a program number, the end word).\n\nWanted, in this order: (1) find a public Sodick source for the LN control's program format, or get the facts from a machine owner as statements about what the control accepts (not as another CAM product's posted program); (2) record what was confirmed and what changed against `docs/decisions/617-sodick-wire-post.md`; (3) change `sodick-wire.cps` (or add a second dialect entry) accordingly, with new goldens.\n\nThe maintainer's answer to the open question on issue 617 (is a machine owner's own program an allowed clean-room source) decides what step 1 may read.\n\nDone means: each item of the \"Unconfirmed\" list of issue 617's PR is marked confirmed, changed or still open, with its source named; the post's header drops \"NOT VERIFIED ON A CONTROL\" only when a machine owner reports a clean dry run.\n\nPart of #617\n",
